#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# surd

#% text
# `surd(x, n)` gives the real n-th root of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For x < 0 and odd n the root is negative; even roots of negative numbers stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
surd(-8, 3)
#% output
#= -2

#% cell
surd(27, 3)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
surd(-2.0, 5)
#% output
#= -1.148698354997035

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The principal power is complex:

#% cell
(-8)^(1/3)
#% output
#= 2*(-1)^(1/3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sqrt`, `abs`
